# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
# libsignal 0.105.2 (Signal Messenger, AGPL-3.0-only), the library Robot to Robot's sessions run on (robot-to-robot-r0.md).
# Signal publishes 0.105.2 only in its own Maven repository, https://build-artifacts.signal.org/libraries/maven/, never on
# Maven Central (which stops at 0.86.5). Robot builds offline from a local copy of these files in third_party/maven-local/
# (git-ignored; tools/fetch_libsignal.sh fills it, robot/README.md "Getting libsignal"), and every one is pinned here.
#
# The AAR's and the jar's lines equal Signal's own .sha256 files for them and the hashes inside their .module files; the
# POM and module files have no .sha256 of their own in the copy R0 made on 21 Oct 2026, so theirs are the files' as R0
# downloaded them. gradle/verification-metadata.xml pins the same six (LibsignalPinsTest checks they agree), so Gradle
# refuses any other bytes; tools/fetch_libsignal.sh refuses them before they reach the repository.
#
# Paths are relative to third_party/maven-local/, so `sha256sum -c` runs there on the lines that start with a hash and "org/".
