#
# The one native library the APK ships: the AAR's jni/arm64-v8a/libsignal_jni.so (123,449,888 bytes, with debug info)
# after `llvm-strip --strip-unneeded` from NDK 27.1.12297006, 9,390,016 bytes. :link's libsignalJni task makes it at
# build time and refuses any other result; tools/verify_apk.sh checks the APK's copy. Never the AAR's
# libsignal_jni_testing.so, its other ABIs, or the client jar's desktop libraries (.so, .dylib, .dll).
